**How to implement.** 'Back up library now…' and 'Restore library…' in the Library window, over the app scope's backup store (001 §C 'Settings'; .spec-md §10: discoverability (both are Library-window buttons), pre-confirmation (Restore library asks), action buttons (the Restore / Cancel pair; restoring the pre-restore backup is the undo); the S2.4 brief). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: the record gains `libraryBackups : LibraryBackupProxy`, its doc one line: the library's backup store, `Backups` beside the database (001 §G). `compose` (step 89) sets it to `LibraryBackupProxy.createInDatabase database locations.backupsFolder (fun () -> LibraryBackupTime DateTime.Now)` (step 86). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs`. (a) `LibraryWindowContext` (`LibraryWindowView.fs:153`) gains `libraryBackups : LibraryBackupProxy` with a one-line doc. (b) Beside `LibraryRemoveGate`, `LibraryRestoreGate` = `NoPendingLibraryRestore` | `PendingLibraryRestore of backups : LibraryBackupName list * pickedOpt : LibraryBackupName option`, documented as the restore panel: closed, or open over the listed backups with the picked one, if any. `LibraryWindowError` (`:70`) gains `LibraryBackupRefusedErr of LibraryBackupError`, and its `caption` renders it through `LibraryBackupError.caption`. (c) `LibraryWindowModel` gains `restoreGate : LibraryRestoreGate` (opening `NoPendingLibraryRestore`) and `backupStatus : ControlCaption option` (opening `None`), each with a one-line doc. (d) `LibraryWindowMsg` gains, each documented: `BackUpLibraryNow`; `RequestLibraryRestore`; `PickLibraryBackup of LibraryBackupName`; `ConfirmLibraryRestore`; `CancelLibraryRestore`. (e) `updateLibraryWindow`. `BackUpLibraryNow` calls `context.libraryBackups.backUpLibrary ()`: `Ok name` sets `backupStatus` to `Library backed up to <name>.` and clears `lastError`; `Error e` sets `lastError` to `LibraryBackupRefusedErr e` and clears `backupStatus`. `RequestLibraryRestore` calls `listBackups ()`: `Ok backups` opens the panel over them with nothing picked, disarms the remove and lifecycle gates and clears `lastError` and `backupStatus`; `Error e` sets `lastError`. `PickLibraryBackup name` picks `name` when the panel is open and lists it, and is inert otherwise. `ConfirmLibraryRestore` with a pick calls `restoreLibrary picked`: `Ok before` closes the panel, clears the selection (`selectedEntryId`, `selectedNodeOpt`, `viewedVersion`), because the restored library may not hold the selected entry, and sets `backupStatus` to `Library restored from <picked>. The library before the restore is backed up as <before>.`; `Error e` sets `lastError` and keeps the panel open. Without a pick, or with the panel closed, it is inert. `CancelLibraryRestore` closes the panel and changes nothing else. A message that arms the remove or the lifecycle gate also closes the panel, so at most one confirmation is ever pending (the rule of `requestLifecycle`, `:540`). (f) The view. In the verbs area, after the entry verbs and in Browse and Select mode alike, `verbButton ConstructorUiId.libraryBackUpNowButton (ControlCaption "Back up library now…")` and `verbButton ConstructorUiId.libraryRestoreButton (ControlCaption "Restore library…")`. While the panel is open, a block carrying `libraryRestorePanel` holds the prompt `Restore the whole library from a backup. The current library is backed up first.`, one `verbButton (ConstructorUiId.libraryBackupRow name.uiKey) (ControlCaption name.value)` per backup in the listed order, the picked one on `positiveBackground` (or `No backup yet.` when there is none), and one row with `actionButton ConstructorUiId.libraryRestoreConfirmButton (ControlCaption "Restore") positiveBackground` and `actionButton ConstructorUiId.libraryRestoreCancelButton (ControlCaption "Cancel") negativeBackground`: the look of the Select / Close pair (`:1013-1014`, `actionButton` at `:1040`), a visible gap and distinct colours. `backupStatus`, when `Some`, shows in a `TextBlock` carrying `libraryBackupStatusText`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `type LibraryBackupName with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey` (the name's text) and `type LibraryBackupError with member this.caption : ControlCaption` (its `describe`), each with a one-line doc. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Library window group (`UiIds.fs:498-523`), under one comment line citing spec 0050 S2.4: `libraryBackUpNowButton` (`"LibraryBackUpNowButton"`), `libraryRestoreButton` (`"LibraryRestoreButton"`), `libraryRestorePanel` (`"LibraryRestorePanel"`), `libraryBackupRow (backup : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$"LibraryBackupRow_{backup.value}"`), `libraryRestoreConfirmButton` (`"LibraryRestoreConfirmButton"`), `libraryRestoreCancelButton` (`"LibraryRestoreCancelButton"`) and `libraryBackupStatusText` (`"LibraryBackupStatusText"`). (5) Threading, so every Library window, opened from the launcher, the strip or a Select session, has the store. `LibraryWindow` (`LibraryWindow.fs:34`) takes `libraryBackups : LibraryBackupProxy` after `categories` and sets the context field. `EditorLaunchers.openLibraryWindow` and `openLibrarySelectWindow` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:158`, `:169`) take it after the `CategoryProxy`, and `EditorLaunchers.defaults` passes it to `LibraryWindow`. `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `libraryBackups : LibraryBackupProxy`, which `initWith` sets to `LibraryBackupProxy.createInMemory ()` for the test scenes as it sets `experimentExport` (`:520`); the strip's `OpenLibraryWindow` (`:1841`) and the Select open (`:3278`) pass `model.libraryBackups`. `Program.fs`'s `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` thread `libraryBackups = context.libraryBackups` by record update beside `sources`, and the launcher's Library button passes `context.libraryBackups`. Every test construction passes one: `LibraryWindowTests`' `stubContext` and its two `LibraryWindow(...)`, `LightSourceEditorTests`' `libraryContext`, `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`' `libraryContext` and `ScrollExtentTests`' `LibraryWindow(...)` pass `LibraryBackupProxy.createInMemory ()`; `WireUiFinalCompositionTests` passes `ctx.libraryBackups`; `MainWorkbenchTests`' recording launchers and `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`' Select-open stub take the extra argument. A doc that lists the window's or the launchers' stores names the backup store in no more words. (6) Tests, in `LibraryWindowTests`. Pure facts over `stubContext` with `LibraryBackupProxy.createInMemory ()`: `the backup and restore UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the seven ids' texts. `BackUpLibraryNow reaches the backup store and shows the backup's name`: after `BackUpLibraryNow`, the store lists one backup and `backupStatus` names it. `a refused backup shows its reason as the window message and no status`: over a backup proxy whose fields answer `LibraryBackupFailedErr`, `lastError` is `LibraryBackupRefusedErr` carrying it and `backupStatus` is `None`. `RequestLibraryRestore opens the panel over the backups, and Restore stays inert until one is picked`: after two backups, `RequestLibraryRestore` opens the panel over both, newest first, and `ConfirmLibraryRestore` before a pick leaves the model unchanged. `confirming a picked backup restores it, names the pre-restore backup, closes the panel and clears the selection`: an entry selected, a backup picked and confirmed; the panel is closed, the selection empty, the store lists the pre-restore backup first, and `backupStatus` names both backups. `Cancel closes the restore panel and restores nothing, and arming Remove closes it too`: `CancelLibraryRestore` closes the panel and the store lists no new backup, and `RequestRemoveSelectedEntry` on a selected sample closes an open panel. And `acceptance: the Library window backs up and restores the app-scope library through its buttons` (trait `ui-smoke`): over `AppContext.create (TestAppScope.fileLocations …)` a `LibraryWindow` composed from the context's stores and `libraryBackups`; clicks on Back up library now…, then a user sample saved through `ctx.samples`, then clicks on Restore library…, the backup's row and Restore: `ctx.samples` no longer resolves the user sample, `libraryBackupStatusText` names the pre-restore backup, and `Backups` holds two backups.

**Acceptance.** After the backup verbs are wired, every Library window, opened from the launcher, the strip or a Select session, MUST carry the app scope's `LibraryBackupProxy` and offer `libraryBackUpNowButton` and `libraryRestoreButton`; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: the Library window backs up and restores the app-scope library through its buttons`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the backup and restore UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `BackUpLibraryNow reaches the backup store and shows the backup's name`, `a refused backup shows its reason as the window message and no status`, `RequestLibraryRestore opens the panel over the backups, and Restore stays inert until one is picked`, `confirming a picked backup restores it, names the pre-restore backup, closes the panel and clears the selection` and `Cancel closes the restore panel and restores nothing, and arming Remove closes it too`, the count rising by 6; and build, elevation and the eleven s11 invariants MUST pass.
